module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.bare_value_admitted_where_optional_is_declared

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { FoundAtAmbiguous, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data bare_value_admitted_where_optional_is_declared: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "bare_value_admitted_where_optional_is_declared" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: FoundAtAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "bare value where an optional is declared: a fn declared `-> T?` whose body produces a bare T, a `data r: T? = <bare T>` row, or a match whose arms mix a bare T with an optional (gunbc.running_release_identity running_release_member_string returned the bare member under `-> String?`). No declared coercion route lifts T into T? (gunbc.design_argument::closed_grounded_substrate, operator ruling 2026-09-26), yet the checker accepted each with zero diagnostics. It is the reverse of optional_admitted_where_a_required_value_is_declared, and a different class from optional_compared_with_required_value, which is the binary-operator seam.",

    "HARM: the Rust emission refused the declared-return and data-row forms downstream as rustc E0308 (`expected Option<T>, found T`), which gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed does not count as a typed refusal; the match form was order-dependent, because the join keeps ONE arm's type, so with `none` listed first the bare arm was never judged against the declared return (join_answers_with_one_arm_others_unjudged).",

    "WALL: v1.compiler.infer optional_at_required_obligation_diags refuses a bare concrete T at PositionDeclaredReturn and PositionDataInitializer (position_forbids_bare_lift) as DeclaredTypeNotInhabited, and match_arm_join_diagnostics refuses a match whose arms mix a bare concrete type with an optional in either arm order, as DeclaredTypeNotInhabited located at the offending arm. Optionality is decided by declared_type_carries_optional, which still decides partly by leaf name: that is the bare-name identity debt routed to the identity-keying lane, carried there and not re-spelled.",

    "EVIDENCE: test.claim.self_host_equality_admission_witness. Reds: a bare return, a bare match arm before a none arm, a bare match arm after a none arm, and a bare data initializer, each refused as blocking DeclaredTypeNotInhabited. Controls: an explicit Present return, an absent return, and a Present-spelled data row, all admitted.",

    "CLAIMED SCOPE (not a rung drop): the match-arm wall does not judge an arm whose whole body is the payload binding of a Present { value: x } pattern, because infer collapses nested optionality (see nested_optional_collapsed_by_infer_carried_by_emission). The exclusion is pinned by an admitted control and a narrowness red in test.claim.self_host_equality_admission_witness.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1 on the Rust emission path (rustc refusal); the interpretation path accepted silently.",

    "RUNG NOW: 3 at three paths only -- the declared return, the data initializer, and the match-arm join -- each with an enrolled red and positive control. A bare T bound to a T? let annotation, record field, call argument or parameter is a different position whose population this change did not measure, and no rung is claimed there; the class's rung is the minimum across its in-scope paths, so it is not claimed beyond those three.",

    "RECEIPT, THE RECORD-FIELD POSITION (2026-11-04, drift-watch run 41453839642, repaired by gunbc#15835; found by deep-otter-318, population audited by still-seal-117): data rows in std.languages wrote bare `\"#\"`/`\"//\"` at record fields declared `String?` (CommentSyntax.line_prefix, block_start, block_end, doc_prefix; ConfigFormat.record; SerializationKnobs.value_quote; Language.naming/types) and extdeps.cloud.gcp.errors gcp_error_example.error.status at `GcpRpcCode?`. v1.compiler.infer admitted them with no diagnostic: declared_type_conformance_diags judges only conformance_ground_type, a Required ground kernel scalar or Required element collection, so a `String?` field is unjudged. INVALID STATE: a bare T at a record field declared T?. HARM: loud but late and non-local. The consumer's `null => ..; binder => ..` arm (std.render comment_prefix_for) refused at runtime with TypeError \"matched an Optional but the value is not an Optional variant: #\" once gunbc#15501 deleted the interpreter bare/Null lift that had hidden the rows, which stopped drift-watch and generated_artifact_gate on main from 2026-11-02. DISTINGUISHING FACTS, executed: a `Present { value: c } / Absent` arm TOLERATES the bare value (it matched gcp_error_example's bare status and passed), so the class is latent wherever that arm form is the only consumer; only the null-and-binder arm form refuses. An authored bare `null` at an Optional position evaluates to Absent (eval_literal LitNull), so it is spelling, not a repair. EVIDENCE: test.claim.languages_optional_rows_witness, RED on the bare rows (TypeError naming `#`, `//`, GcpRpcCodePermissionDenied), 7 claims GREEN after. REPAIR: at the source rows (explicit Present/Absent, gunbc.design_ruling explicit_present_is_the_authoring_policy), not a front-end lift. NOT ADDED: a v1 checker refusal at the record-field position, because v1 is semantics-frozen under gunbc.v1.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing and v2.std.inhabitance declared_type_inhabitance judges the lift direction natively; the rung at this position therefore stays below the ceiling on v1 and is the v2 route's to carry. POPULATION AUDITED, bounded git grep over dag/extdeps and dag/std (not a census): MarkupFormat.code_fence rows (std.languages and extdeps.languages.markdown) remain bare with no consumer by grep; bare `null` rows in std.languages and `value_quote: null` in gunbc.host.host_runner_memory_cap_plan_emit and gunbc.runner.runner_deploy_emit are Absent already; other modules and `?` fields are unknown.",

    "CEILING: 4 is not attainable while the surface can spell a bare value beside an optional declaration. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER for the unclaimed positions: measuring the corpus population at let, field, argument and parameter positions and enrolling their reds, which is possible now and unbuilt; and for the leaf-name optionality decision, declaration-decided optionality in the checker.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
